    "hoop": {
      "word": "HOOP",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "A pliant strip of wood or metal bent in a circular form, and united at the ends, for holding together the staves of casks, tubs, etc.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "A ring; a circular band; anything resembling a hoop, as the cylinder (cheese hoop) in which the curd is pressed in making cheese.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "A circle, or combination of circles, of thin whalebone, metal, or other elastic material, used for expanding the skirts of ladies' dresses; crinoline; -- used chiefly in the plural. Though stiff with hoops, and armed with ribs of whale. Pope.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "A quart pot; -- so called because originally bound with hoops, like a barrel. Also, a portion of the contents measured by the distance between the hoops. [Obs.]",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "An old measure of capacity, variously estimated at from one to four pecks. [Eng.] Halliwell. Bulge hoop, Chine hoop, Quarter hoop, the hoop nearest the middle of a cask, that nearest the end, and the intermediate hoop between these two, respectively. outside. notching and interlocking them. woman's dress; -- called also hoop petticoat. States (Abaster erythrogrammus); -- so called from the mistaken notion that it curves itself into a hoop, taking its tail into its mouth, and rolls along with great velocity. of the Mahogany family.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "To bind or fasten with hoops; as, to hoop a barrel or puncheon.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To clasp; to encircle; to surround. Shak.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To utter a loud cry, or a sound imitative of the word, by way of call or pursuit; to shout. [Usually written whoop.]",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To whoop, as in whooping cough. See Whoop. Hooping cough. (Med.) See Whooping cough.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To drive or follow with a shout. \"To be hooped out of Rome.\" Shak.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To call by a shout or peculiar cry.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "A shout; a whoop, as in whooping cough.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "(Zoöl.)",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "The hoopoe. See Hoopoe.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        }
      ],
